  "$comment": "DEVELOPMENT descriptor for the deberta_decision family (hfmodels-litert, not in the bundled catalog). Generated by tools/hfmodels_descriptor.py from the Hub at the pinned revision: every file's bytes and sha256 are the Hub's. The device gate side-loads the published files from /data/local/tmp/hfmodels/open-decision (DebertaDecisionDeviceTest). The draft for the repo's own hfmodels.json (without the top-level revision). The published three (s256_wfp16, s512_wfp16, and s256_npu_wfp16 since 26a2b642) and one development variant: s256_fp32 is the float32 graph the published S256 wfp16 file was cast from, a local file that is not on the Hub (re-exported 2026-10-04 with the conversion run's scripts/export.py --seq 256: bytes and sha256 equal the 2026-10-01 export record, and its float16 cast is byte-identical to the Hub's deberta_v3_large_decision_s256_wfp16.tflite), for the CPU fp32 row. s256_npu_wfp16 is the S256 graph re-authored for the Qualcomm HTP: OD-D of the typed-decisions speed rounds (r16, 2026-10-04; r21 replaced r12's OD-B with it): a -1e4 attention-mask constant, LayerNorm power-of-two pre-scale on all 49 norms (k per norm: the 24 FFN-output norms from the fp32 range profile, 1 to 5 with L22's 0 raised to 1; the embedding norm and the 24 attention-output norms 1), FC1 of all 24 FFNs split into two FULLY_CONNECTED joined by CONCATENATION; exact in fp32, the same I/O contract, table and tokenizer as s256_wfp16. Published in the repo at 26a2b642 (r21; the bytes and sha256 of r16's export), with an npu profile asked for by name (BackendPolicy.Require, no fallback; gpu stays the default, at fp16_with_fp32_accum as the catalog).",
